.\" $GergiOS$
.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt RPCAPD 8
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm rpcapd
.Nd remote packet capture daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 46dh
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl u Ar username
.Op Fl P Ar password
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a daemon that implements the Remote Packet Capture Protocol (RPCAP),
allowing remote clients such as Wireshark to capture packets from
network interfaces on this host using the
.Ic rpcap://
protocol.
.Pp
The daemon listens for incoming TCP connections (default port 2002),
authenticates the client, and serves packet capture data via the
RPCAP protocol.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 4
Listen on IPv4 only.
.It Fl 6
Listen on IPv6 only.
.It Fl d
Run in foreground (do not daemonize).
.It Fl u Ar username
Require this username for authentication.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl P
(if one is specified, both should be).
.It Fl P Ar password
Require this password for authentication.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl u
(if one is specified, both should be).
.It Fl p Ar port
Listen on the specified TCP port instead of the default 2002.
.It Fl h
Display help and exit.
.El
.Sh PROTOCOL
The RPCAP protocol works as follows:
.Bl -enum
.It
The client connects to port 2002 and sends an
.Dv AUTH_REQ
message.
The server supports both null authentication (no password, default)
and password authentication (see
.Fl u
and
.Fl P
flags).
.It
After authentication, the client sends a
.Dv FINDALLIF_REQ
to list available network interfaces.
.It
To start capturing, the client sends
.Dv OPEN_REQ
(interface name) followed by
.Dv STARTCAP_REQ
(snapshot length, timeout, flags).
.It
Captured packets are streamed as
.Dv PACKET
messages over the same TCP connection.
.It
The client ends the capture with
.Dv ENDCAP_REQ
or closes the connection with
.Dv CLOSE .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/bpf -compact
.It Pa /dev/bpf
Berkeley Packet Filter clone device
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run the daemon in the foreground on the default port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rpcapd -d
.Ed
.Pp
Run with password authentication:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rpcapd -d -u admin -P secret123
.Ed
.Pp
Run on a custom port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rpcapd -p 2004
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pcapng 1 ,
.Xr tcpdump 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in GergiOS.
